course: dictionary
lesson: 12397
title: Curative: words about making people well
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Curative» comes from «cure», and it means able to make an illness go away. A curative treatment is one that really does cure you. «The doctor gave him a curative medicine, and the infection went away.» The clue is the medicine that made the infection go away.
explain: The word also means something put right, not just stopped from getting worse. «The mechanic's repair was curative, so the car ran smoothly again.» The car was fixed, not just kept from breaking more.
explain: Compare curative with preventive. A preventive treatment stops you getting the illness in the first place, like a vaccine. A curative treatment helps once you already have it. Two words that are close in meaning can have very different jobs.
fact: Curative means able to cure an illness or make someone healthy again.
fact: «Preventive» means meant to stop something happening, such as an illness.
fact: As a rare noun, «a curative» means a medicine or treatment that cures.
fact: «Curative powers» means the ability to heal, as people once believed some springs and herbs had.
fact: In stories, people believed in curative powers, but a story is not a proof that a spring can cure anything.
exercise: «The doctor gave her a curative medicine, and the infection went away.» What does curative mean here? | Very expensive | Sold only in shops | Made of wood | *Able to cure an illness
exercise: In health lessons, one treatment stops you getting an illness and another cures it. Which word means the one that stops you getting it? | Ancient | Curative | Glum | *Preventive
exercise: «The old story said the healing spring had curative powers.» Find and copy the word that means able to cure. | said | *curative | story | spring
test: «The healers believed the herbs had curative properties.» What does curative properties mean? | Qualities that make tea taste nice | Qualities that stop plants being picked | Qualities that make plants grow faster | *Qualities that can cure illness
test: Curative can also be a noun. What does «a curative» mean? | A bandage for a small cut | A test to measure your height | A doctor who works at night | *A medicine or treatment that cures
exam: The vaccine is preventive, but the antibiotic is ... because it cures the infection. | barely | *curative | ancient | preventive
